  "name": "Create and approve Xero invoices from Pipedrive deals with Slack",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "7f7012f6-003f-4244-9419-2257f56fa528",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -656,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## Deal-to-invoice automation (CRM \u2192 Xero)\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow listens for Pipedrive deal updates and continues only when a deal enters the Closed Won stage. It retrieves the related person, finds or creates the matching Xero contact, builds invoice line items from the deal products, and creates a draft invoice in Xero. The draft is sent to Slack for approval; approved invoices are authorised and emailed when a contact email exists, while rejected or non-email cases are reported in Slack.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect Pipedrive credentials for the trigger and CRM lookup nodes.\n- Connect Xero credentials or configure OAuth headers for the Xero contact and invoice API requests.\n- Connect Slack credentials and choose the channel or approvers for the approval and notification messages.\n- Set the Workflow Config values, including Xero organization ID, Closed Won stage ID, sales account code, and tax type.\n- Verify the Pipedrive deal/person fields and product fields used to build contact data and invoice line items.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the Closed Won stage filter, invoice account code, tax type, Slack approver/channel, and line-item mapping logic to match the sales process and accounting setup."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f3a888e0-67d4-42d5-a09e-b2773789310d",
